{"uuid":"E830F46E-7C18-5F57-A4D1-CC32B311EAD7","name":"Cilantro Lime Taco Bowls","serves":10,"duration":20,"cookingDuration":55,"defaultScale":1,"isPublicRecipe":false,"folderIDs":[],"ingredients":[{"uuid":"F3C436B8-4634-5904-B064-F47CD6610F90","order":0,"ingredient":{"uuid":"7159C11A-24D4-54B9-9954-0778D5829618","name":"ground beef (90/10) or ground turkey"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"POUND","amount":5}},{"uuid":"4E1CDAC5-DF77-55B7-B329-63029386B331","order":1,"ingredient":{"uuid":"4127D2DC-D7B8-5C0E-9603-D7700CDC34C2","name":"packets low-sodium taco seasoning (220 mg per 2 tsp)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":3}},{"uuid":"E00B7A2C-183C-52F5-945E-B9D8D0F40975","order":2,"ingredient":{"uuid":"A461D129-E763-5F93-AEBC-7D177D4C00B2","name":"chili powder"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TABLESPOON","amount":1}},{"uuid":"6C680146-E2D0-5A16-B659-EE4D43F30C39","order":3,"ingredient":{"uuid":"6D3C6CC4-2ECF-581D-BABD-301BB0DB997B","name":"ground cumin"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TEASPOON","amount":1.5}},{"uuid":"701C1D0D-B129-50D6-BE87-11D0589118C7","order":4,"ingredient":{"uuid":"6C21BEA2-EEA9-5E90-AB41-42933C692365","name":"paprika"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TEASPOON","amount":0.75}},{"uuid":"D2CC4BD6-5F40-5119-800E-A095F9CBABAE","order":5,"ingredient":{"uuid":"B9747176-15EC-5A56-9B7C-C0C2914D7E0C","name":"garlic powder"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TEASPOON","amount":0.5}},{"uuid":"6753520B-012D-5806-AD68-97D5268C249B","order":6,"ingredient":{"uuid":"BB109108-CE3D-5115-B6E2-7CF74E2668EA","name":"onion powder"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TEASPOON","amount":0.5}},{"uuid":"9E5E2A28-9D46-595A-8782-D0ADF13F4CBD","order":7,"ingredient":{"uuid":"941912A2-8101-5159-AC26-081CDB89AD26","name":"dried oregano"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TEASPOON","amount":0.25}},{"uuid":"C2C3493F-B32E-594A-B1FE-8217CCD50F84","order":8,"ingredient":{"uuid":"E388E846-60C7-5C30-AA2F-DE6B3B6FFF74","name":"cans black beans"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":3}},{"uuid":"AC2AE4FC-4DE8-5A97-B932-BF117B8DB2EE","order":9,"ingredient":{"uuid":"CC8627AF-79AF-5549-A1D6-D1F01ECDC8EC","name":"jasmine rice (dry)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":3.5}},{"uuid":"AC14D483-8FA4-5336-8850-C8F281B09021","order":10,"ingredient":{"uuid":"6C8F980F-85AF-5B6F-8779-D4D498B6CFE6","name":"limes, juiced (or 3–4 tbsp bottled)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":3}},{"uuid":"298711AF-B137-5FC6-AB74-09ECD392D797","order":11,"ingredient":{"uuid":"EBC8C9E4-CBAF-5AB4-A93A-1D9B1840CC17","name":"bunch fresh cilantro, chopped (optional)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":0.5}},{"uuid":"73EC6512-F430-5320-820F-65594A36A677","order":12,"ingredient":{"uuid":"81A8E379-6CA6-5890-B38D-FE5C334C1A4C","name":"bell peppers"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":6}},{"uuid":"28A0B2B1-C2BD-5B52-8AB3-8972DD48F8B2","order":13,"ingredient":{"uuid":"524D9041-D2C8-5C35-9F03-76E2B705E0F0","name":"large onion"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":1}},{"uuid":"EF4C9AF1-5E57-5D57-8E8F-607337BAB5C0","order":14,"ingredient":{"uuid":"3D8811C8-31C2-5FDB-80DC-36EB8F883DF7","name":"bag frozen sweet corn (12–16 oz)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":1}},{"uuid":"795B7B5C-454D-5E1E-8080-C540F70F69F6","order":15,"ingredient":{"uuid":"A6CE6874-93FF-55D1-87D9-6A5C816C208D","name":"Olive oil, as needed"}},{"uuid":"B3EA480F-B2F9-5919-A528-153DD825DF3D","order":16,"ingredient":{"uuid":"BC34F11D-B9EC-5156-9FB6-660DAC3E746F","name":"Shredded cheese, salsa, sour cream (added fresh when eating)"}}],"steps":[{"uuid":"F8E336FC-25D4-57DB-A563-5CED3A91A357","order":0,"step":"Rinse 3 ½ cups jasmine rice 2–3 times until the water runs mostly clear. Add to the Instant Pot with 3 ½ cups water (1:1).","isSection":false},{"uuid":"23D89A46-7593-55FD-A9E0-60033FFFB156","order":1,"step":"Confirm the valve is set to SEALING and the float valve pops up. Pressure Cook (Manual) on High for 3 minutes, natural release 10 minutes, then quick release.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"5394414D-EA70-59DC-A9C5-5AFE70002CD6","order":2,"step":"Fluff the rice, then stir in the lime juice and chopped cilantro. Leave the lid off to cool. Add the lime after cooking, not before.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"E9A00228-C579-54E4-9A68-E2F57CEB5765","order":3,"step":"Heat a large pan over medium-high. Add 5 lbs ground beef, breaking it up as it cooks. Brown 10–12 minutes until no pink remains and it reaches 165°F. Work in 2 batches if the pan is crowded — crowding steams the meat instead of browning it.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"A632D338-4C61-5E50-81B0-BA25563A54A8","order":4,"step":"Drain the excess fat thoroughly. Beef renders noticeably more than turkey, and skipping this makes the bowls greasy by day 3.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"648BD883-48C8-50D7-B835-D0C5568466CC","order":5,"step":"Add 3 packets low-sodium taco seasoning plus the bulk spices — 1 tbsp chili powder, 1 ½ tsp cumin, ¾ tsp paprika, ½ tsp garlic powder, ½ tsp onion powder, ¼ tsp oregano. That blend stands in for a fourth packet.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"04EC6A90-D5AF-5094-8AD5-0C7B2415ABF9","order":6,"step":"Add the water called for on 3 packets plus another ¼ cup for the bulk spices. Simmer 2–3 minutes until thickened. Taste and add salt if it reads flat — that is the point of the swap, the salt is now yours to set rather than the packet's.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"2E375031-1BD6-5699-A32B-F05C1CF5F576","order":7,"step":"In a separate pan, heat a little olive oil. Add the diced bell peppers and onion and sauté 6–8 minutes until softened.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"706F8EA9-2630-5EAC-A5D4-500CE779E9C5","order":8,"step":"Add the frozen corn for the last 3–4 minutes. Let it pick up a few golden char spots for a fire-roasted flavor.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"32136017-0E02-50DF-BB8E-EE564BD62DE3","order":9,"step":"Rinse and drain 3 cans black beans, then warm them in a small pot or the microwave. Rinsing cuts sodium and stops the cloudy can liquid from making the bowls mushy.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"351F3F74-533D-5955-BB2B-F4EC2C785D89","order":10,"step":"Let the meat, rice, veggies, and beans cool 10 minutes before portioning. Sealing hot food causes condensation and sogginess.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"38A74339-0D48-558A-98BA-0F2654CDCBCB","order":11,"step":"Assembly line across 10 open containers: 170 g meat, then 150 g rice, then 80 g beans, then 110 g veg and corn. No separate sauce container — the taco seasoning is already in the meat.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"F77AE33B-B1B7-5E98-A714-BB37D68C208E","order":12,"step":"Label with a dry-erase marker. 6 containers to the fridge for the first half of the week, 4 to the freezer. Move freezer containers to the fridge the night before eating.","isSection":false}],"notes":"DIALED-IN — v4, last cooked 2026-07-26\n\nPER CONTAINER (10 total)\n  meat: 170 g\n  rice: 150 g\n  beans: 80 g\n  veg: 110 g\n  total: 510 g\n\nSTORAGE: 6 fridge, 4 freezer\nFreezer containers move to the fridge the night before eating.\n\nFRESH TOPPINGS — NEVER PACKED: shredded cheese, salsa, sour cream\nAdded at eating time only.\n\nLessons from real cook sessions:\n\nProtein was bumped from 3.5 lbs to 5 lbs — 120 g per container was too light to stay full through the afternoon. Bell peppers shrink hard when cooked; 3 peppers only yielded ~170 g total, so buy 6. Rice at 3 ½ cups dry yields ~1500 g cooked, which lands 150 g per container.\n\nAldi is frequently out of fresh limes and cilantro. Bottled lime juice is a fine fallback and the dish still works with the cilantro skipped entirely.\n\nDouble-check the Instant Pot valve is on SEALING before walking away. This has gone wrong before.\n\nCold toppings — cheese, salsa, sour cream — go on fresh at eating time, never packed into the containers.\n\nThis is the cheapest prep in the rotation and the only one requiring no oven.\n\nSodium, resolved in v4 but not yet cooked. It ran ~950 mg per container on\n4 regular packets, and the packets were ~560 mg of that. Aldi's low-sodium\nblend is 220 mg per 2 tsp against roughly 300 for regular.\n\nSwapping all four to low-sodium is not enough on its own — it only gets to\n~804 mg, a 16% cut, because the packet count matters more than the\nformulation. v4 uses 3 low-sodium packets plus a tablespoon-scale bulk blend\nstanding in for the fourth, which projects to ~700 mg.\n\nOnly the seasoning changed, so the observed yields above still hold. The\nsodium figure has always been `estimated`, so recalculating it is legitimate —\nbut **taste this before treating 700 as settled**, and note whether it needs\nsalt added back. Half a teaspoon across the whole batch is only ~116 mg per\ncontainer and would still land near 713.\n\nEventually worth mixing the blend in bulk and dropping packets entirely, which\nwould put this near 390 mg. Two things to sort first: a jar to keep it in, and\na cornstarch slurry to replace the thickening the packets provide — that is\nwhat step 7's simmer relies on, and it is the reason not to jump straight to\nan all-bulk version on the fastest recipe in the rotation.\n\nOpen item: the vegetable arithmetic does not close. Using only measured\nfigures — 57 g per cooked pepper and ~80 g per cooked onion, both now in\n`docs/standing-parameters.md` — 6 peppers plus 1 onion plus a 12–16 oz bag of\ncorn comes to roughly 760–880 g. That is 76–87 g per container, not the 110 g\nthis recipe claims, a shortfall of 220–340 g per batch. Either the veg was\nnever weighed on the sessions behind this recipe, or more onion went in than\nthe ingredient list records. Weigh the combined veg before portioning on the\nnext cook and correct whichever end is wrong. Nothing here has been changed\nwithout a scale behind it.","neutritionalInfo":"Serving Size: 1 container,\nCalories: 700 kcal,\nProtein: 52 g,\nCarbohydrates: 60 g,\nFat: 25 g,\nFiber: 9 g,\nSodium: 700 mg,\nSugar: 2 g","sourceName":"ten-containers","webLink":"https://zjbecker32.github.io/ten-containers/recipes/cilantro-lime-taco-bowls/","tags":[],"images":[]}